utes a routine (release‑move, swing, transition) wearing a Union‑Jack‑styled leotard. The pink competition floor and landing mats are clearly in view. |\n| **023‑030** | **Judges & Officials** – seated at the scoring table to the side of the bars. | Judges watch the routine, holding score cards and a tablet; the panel is recognizable as the Olympic judging crew. |\n| **055‑061** | **Scoreboard Close‑up** – digital display on the far wall. | The board cycles through live scores: athlete names, country codes, and point totals (e.g., “Aliya\u202fMustafina\u202f16.133\u202f–\u202fGold”). |\n| **062‑069** | **Gymnast – Various competitors (CHN, RUS, USA)** – mid‑performance on the bars. | Each athlete is shown in turn, flipping and transitioning while the camera tracks their motion from the bar to the landing mat. Their leotards reflect national colours (e.g., blue‑pink for China, red for Russia). |\n| **070‑090** | **Audience Reaction** – cutaways to the crowd. | Fans cheer, wave flags, and hold up signs as each routine finishes; the atmosphere is vibrant and live. |\n| **1965‑1996** | **Continued Competition Shots** – mixture of close‑ups on athletes, judges, and scoreboard. | The sequence repeats the pattern above: a gymnast launches from the bars, judges record scores, the scoreboard updates, and the crowd reacts. |\n\n### Character & Element Tracking  \n\n- **Gymnasts** (e.g., Elizabeth\u202fTweddle, Aliya\u202fMustafina, other finalists) – appear in frames **021‑030**, **062‑069**, **1965‑1996**; perform on the uneven bars, wear nation‑specific leotards, and land on the pink floor.  \n- **Judges/Officials** – appear in frames **023‑030**, **1965‑1996**; seated at the scoring table, observing performances, and entering scores.  \n- **Spectators** – present throughout frames **001‑020**, **055‑061**, **070‑090**, **1965‑1996**; fill the arena stands, wave flags, and react audibly.  \n- **Scoreboard** – visible in frames **002‑006**, **055‑061**, **1965‑1996**; displays event title and real‑time results.  \n- **Equipment** – uneven bars, pink competition floor, landing mats, and the judges’ table are consistently in view across the whole segment.\n\n### Cohesive Narrative  \n\nThe clip opens with a sweeping view of a packed Olympic arena, introducing the atmosphere of a live, high‑stakes gymnastics competition. The camera then zooms onto the first finalist, Elizabeth\u202fTweddle, as she executes a precise routine on the uneven bars, her British‑styled leotard standing out against the apparatus. Judges seated nearby watch closely, ready to record the score that will appear moments later on the large digital scoreboard. The scoreboard flashes the athletes’ names, national codes, and current points, confirming the competition’s real‑time nature. Subsequent frames follow other finalists from China, Russia, the United States, and elsewhere, each delivering their own high‑difficulty sequences while the audience reacts with cheers and national‑pride gestures. Throughout the segment, the recurring visual loop—athlete on bars → judges observing → scoreboard updating → crowd response—reinforces that this is a live broadcast of an Olympic gymnastics event, not a narrated documentary or instructional piece.', 'failed_images': [('/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/rp4NKWb7dXk/frames/frame_0000.jpg', 'File not found'), ('/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/rp4NKWb7dXk/frames/frame_1997.jpg', 'File not found')]}
